  "question_stem": "A particle $P$ moves in a straight line starting from a point $O$ and comes to rest 35 s later. At time $t$ s after leaving $O$, the velocity $v$ $\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$ of $P$ is given by\n\n$$v = \\frac{4}{5}t^2 \\qquad 0 \\le t \\le 5,$$\n$$v = 2t + 10 \\qquad 5 \\le t \\le 15,$$\n$$v = a + bt^2 \\qquad 15 \\le t \\le 35,$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants such that $a > 0$ and $b < 0$.",
  "context_texts": [
    "$a=49$ and $b=-0.04$",
    "$v=0.8t^2$ for $0\\le t\\le5$; the graph is a straight line from $(5,20)$ to $(15,40)$; and $v=49-0.04t^2$ for $15\\le t\\le35$"
  ],
